  "verbalization": "Isoflurane, a member of the organofluorine compound class, is linked to Kcnk18 through its interaction with Desflurane, which binds to the same molecular target. This relationship is supported by multiple paths, all of which highlight a shared dependency on Desflurane as a mediator. The evidence suggests that Isoflurane, through its inclusion in the anesthetic agent category, indirectly influences Kcnk18 via Desflurane. The lowest common ancestor of Isoflurane and Desflurane, both classified as organofluorine compounds, reinforces the biochemical link between these entities. The consistent presence of Desflurane as a binding partner for Kcnk18 across different pathways underscores a potential mechanism involving anesthetic agents in the regulation of Kcnk18. The integration of these findings suggests that Isoflurane may exert its effects on Kcnk18 through a pathway involving Desflurane, though the exact molecular mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
